// The AST-store leg of the init chain (init_nodes/2/3, this file's other
// neighbour): every stage keeps its own exported lists and none of the init
// functions call each other, so all fourteen have to be named somewhere.
// Three actions to a block makes that a chain rather than a list, and this
// is the one leg every case that touches a node needs, so it lives beside
// the three functions it calls rather than beside boot_b's chain
// (c2id/emit/gen/out/top/init/boot.id), which lex/ and parse/ never call.

boot_a() {
  init_nodes();
  init_nodes2();
  init_nodes3();
} return void;
():() then calls init_nodes:()
():() then calls init_nodes3:()
